# LUCI messaging voice

Canonical source: **Messaging guide** → Voice & tone → *Engine and verbs — not layers.*

## Don’t

Never use **layer** as a noun for LUCI (orchestration layer, application layer, “one layer for…”). Describing layers in the **client’s** accumulated stack is fine.

## Leading choices (not the only choices)

- **Orchestration engine** — positioning, tagline
- **LUCI orchestrates…** — headlines, capability copy

Also fine when they fit better: **runs, operates, integrates, consolidates, refines, platform, infrastructure**.

## Watch repetition

If **engine** or **orchestrates** appears more than once in a short passage (deck section, PDF page, email), rotate to a precise alternative. Same word three times reads like a crutch.

## Spelling & terms

- **Always write “A/V”** — never “AV” or “A-V” — in body copy, headlines, labels, captions, alt text, and diagrams.

Voice patches re-apply after Word sync via `transform-messaging-html.mjs`.
